<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<cfsSimulation xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
               xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation ../../../../../share/xml/CFS-Simulation/CFS.xsd"
               xmlns="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation">

  <documentation>
    <title>Contact with a non-zero reference gap: interference fit carrying an external load</title>
    <authors><author>kroppert</author></authors>
    <date>2026-08-06</date>
    <keywords><keyword>contact</keyword></keywords>
    <references>none</references>
    <isVerified>no</isVerified>
    <description>
      The ContactPatchTest3d load case on the ContactOverlap3d mesh, where the two bodies
      interpenetrate by 0.1 as meshed. The reference gap is therefore g_0 = -0.1 instead of 0,
      which is what this test exists for: the constant part of the penalty residual, -eps_N *
      g_0 * INT N_D^T n dG, is a right-hand-side vector no stiffness matrix can produce, and it
      carries the entire initial load.

      Equilibrium still fixes the answer exactly -- the interface is the only load path to the
      support -- so the expected pressure, total force and penetration are identical to
      ContactPatchTest3d despite the completely different reference configuration.

      Omitting the g_0 term does not crash: it silently solves the problem of two bodies whose
      as-meshed interpenetration is stress free, giving a pressure three orders of magnitude too
      high. That is the failure this test catches.
    </description>
  </documentation>

  <fileFormats>
    <input>
      <hdf5 fileName="ContactInterference3d.h5" linearizeEntities="__none__"/>
    </input>
    <output><hdf5/></output>
    <materialData file="mat.xml" format="xml"/>
  </fileFormats>

  <domain geometryType="3d">
    <regionList>
      <region name="master_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
      <region name="slave_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
    </regionList>
    <surfRegionList>
      <surfRegion name="master_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="slave_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="top"/>
      <surfRegion name="bottom"/>
    </surfRegionList>
  </domain>

  <fePolynomialList>
    <Lagrange><gridOrder/></Lagrange>
  </fePolynomialList>

  <integrationSchemeList>
    <scheme>
      <method>Gauss</method>
      <order>4</order>
      <mode>absolute</mode>
    </scheme>
  </integrationSchemeList>

  <sequenceStep>
    <analysis><static/></analysis>

    <pdeList>
      <mechanic subType="3d">
        <regionList>
          <region name="master_elem"/>
          <region name="slave_elem"/>
        </regionList>

        <!-- initialGapHandling="fromMesh" is the whole point: the as-meshed overlap of 0.1
             is kept as a real interference, not neutralized. Switching this to "zero" turns
             the test into ContactPatchTest3d. -->
        <contactList>
          <contactPair name="cube_contact"
                       primarySurface="master_iface"
                       secondarySurface="slave_iface"
                       slidingType="small"
                       normalPenalty="100"
                       initialGapHandling="fromMesh"
                       integrationOrder="2"/>
        </contactList>

        <bcsAndLoads>
          <!-- lower body fully supported -->
          <fix name="bottom">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/><comp dof="z"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- upper body: suppress the lateral rigid-body modes only. Its z support comes
               exclusively from the contact interface. -->
          <fix name="top">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/>
          </fix>
          <pressure name="top" value="1e6"/>
        </bcsAndLoads>

        <storeResults>
          <nodeResult type="mechDisplacement"><allRegions/></nodeResult>
        </storeResults>
      </mechanic>
    </pdeList>

    <linearSystems>
      <system>
        <solutionStrategy>
          <standard>
            <setup idbcHandling="penalty"/>
            <matrix storage="sparseNonSym" reordering="noReordering"/>
            <nonLinear method="newton" logging="no">
              <lineSearch type="none"/>
              <incStopCrit>1e-9</incStopCrit>
              <resStopCrit>1e-9</resStopCrit>
              <maxNumIters>20</maxNumIters>
            </nonLinear>
          </standard>
        </solutionStrategy>
        <solverList><directLU/></solverList>
      </system>
    </linearSystems>

  </sequenceStep>
</cfsSimulation>
